<p>(a) Earnings for the six months ended June 30, 1997 include (1) a one-time non-cash stock option charge of $22.5 million related to the conversion of stock options at the time of the initial public offering, (2) an income tax benefit recorded in the first quarter of $23.2 million reflecting the recoverability of a portion of the net operating loss carryforward, and (3) a pre-tax charge of $14.2 million for the write-off of unamortized debt financing costs and premiums associated with the redemption of the 13% discount debentures and the 11% notes.</p>
<p>(b) The decrease in weighted average shares in 1997 resulted from the repurchase of approximately 4.3 million shares in July 1996, net of 3.7 million shares issued in February 1997 in the initial public offering. If the initial public offering had occurred as of January 1, 1997, the weighted average shares in 1997 would have been 20.5 million.</p>
